IMPORT policy

-- The nine benchmark queries (Kant et al. 2025, Appendix A.2).
--
-- Standing preamble applied to every query below: assume all other
-- conditions are met and no other exclusions apply, i.e. every fact not
-- mentioned by a given query is set here to whichever value keeps that
-- unrelated condition satisfied / that unrelated exclusion untriggered.
-- Also assumed throughout: the agreement has been signed and the premium
-- has been paid on time (policy.l4 encodes no rule for either, per the
-- task instructions, so there is no field for them here).

§ `The nine benchmark queries`

-- Q1: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while
-- doing my duty as a firefighter?
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                IS 40
    `hospitalization month`                                 IS 0
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`  IS TRUE
    `event arose out of skydiving`                          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the military`            IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`          IS TRUE
    `event arose out of service in the police`              IS FALSE
    `wellness visit confirmation month`                     IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`   IS TRUE
    `claimant committed fraud`                              IS FALSE
    `claimant made a misrepresentation`                     IS FALSE
    `claimant materially withheld information`              IS FALSE
    `dispute exists between the parties`                    IS FALSE
    `valid arbitration award has been issued`               IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q1


