#EVAL `covered` q4


-- Q5: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face
-- to show off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or
-- misrepresentation?
--
-- Judgment call: the injury here results from a deliberate act (throwing
-- the punch) but not from a deliberate intent to injure oneself -- the
-- claimant meant to show off, not to hospitalize themselves. Under the
-- ordinary "accidental result" reading of accident insurance (the
-- unintended consequence of a voluntary act still counts as accidental),
-- and given the contract's §2.1 exclusions do not list self-inflicted or
-- intentional injury at all, this is encoded as an accidental injury.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                IS 40
    `hospitalization month`                                 IS 0
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`  IS TRUE
    `event arose out of skydiving`                          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the military`            IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the police`              IS FALSE
    `wellness visit confirmation month`                     IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`   IS TRUE
    `claimant committed fraud`                              IS FALSE
    `claimant made a misrepresentation`                     IS FALSE
    `claimant materially withheld information`              IS FALSE
    `dispute exists between the parties`                    IS FALSE
    `valid arbitration award has been issued`               IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q5


