-- Q8: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a
-- military training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the
-- policy term, and I did not commit fraud?
--
-- Judgment call: "the hospitalization occurred within the policy term" is
-- encoded by giving `hospitalization month` a value within the one-year
-- (12-month) term, since policy.l4 tests term-membership via that same
-- relative-month field rather than via a separate primitive fact.
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                IS 40
    `hospitalization month`                                 IS 0
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`  IS TRUE
    `event arose out of skydiving`                          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the military`            IS TRUE
    `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the police`              IS FALSE
    `wellness visit confirmation month`                     IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`   IS TRUE
    `claimant committed fraud`                              IS FALSE
    `claimant made a misrepresentation`                     IS FALSE
    `claimant materially withheld information`              IS FALSE
    `dispute exists between the parties`                    IS FALSE
    `valid arbitration award has been issued`               IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q8


-- Q9: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me
-- in the ankle, proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after the
-- effective date, and I was serving as a police officer at the time of
-- hospitalization?
--
-- Judgment call: §2.1(4) excludes an event "arising directly or indirectly
-- out of ... service in the police" -- a causal requirement, not a mere
-- status requirement. Being employed as a police officer "at the time of
-- hospitalization" does not by itself mean the injury arose out of that
-- service; a son biting his parent's ankle is a domestic incident with no
-- causal connection to police duties. So the police-service exclusion flag
-- is set FALSE here even though the claimant's occupation is a police
-- officer.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                IS 40
    `hospitalization month`                                 IS 0
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`  IS TRUE
    `event arose out of skydiving`                          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the military`            IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`          IS FALSE
    `event arose out of service in the police`              IS FALSE
    `wellness visit confirmation month`                     IS JUST 6
    `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`   IS TRUE
    `claimant committed fraud`                              IS FALSE
    `claimant made a misrepresentation`                     IS FALSE
    `claimant materially withheld information`              IS FALSE
    `dispute exists between the parties`                    IS FALSE
    `valid arbitration award has been issued`               IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q9
